  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&apos;s Media Watchdog (WMW Project): Advancing Diversity, Equality, and Inclusion in the Election Coverage Reporting</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this project Konde.co seeks to strengthen the role of women&apos;s media as a watchdog to ensure that the 2024 elections and the governance during the period beyond will be inclusive or involve women and vulnerable groups, not only increasing their participation as election participants (voters) but also allows women&apos;s representation and vulnerable groups getting publications of their stories and victories as well as pushing policies that are inclusive and anti-discrimination. In order to achieve these goals, Konde.co sets three strategies: the first strategy is for Women&apos;s Media to have election coverage guidelines for women and vulnerable groups, the second is to strengthen women&apos;s media and their journalist&#x2019;s  knowledge and strengthen the collaboration on inclusivity and diversity issues. The last strategy is strengthening women&#x2019;s media public education on inclusivity and diversity toward election.</narrative>
  </description>
